      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bc63165b150d502fa6164e3|full_name}: Rly? For now I can only get bones' positions/rotations, but I still don't have access to the object itself. So I believe that \"attachment\" you meant is just manual repositioning an object to the mentioned bones' pos/rotation. But that is not actually what I meant in the topic. At least, you can still manually track the player itself by getting their position/rotation.",
